I'll provide a basic example of the requested C program. This code uses the `sys/ioctl.h`, `fcntl.h`, `unistd.h`, `stdio.h`, `stdlib.h`, `time.h`, and `signal.h` libraries for system calls and error handling. It also uses the `spidev` library for communicating with the MCP3008 ADC.

Please note that this code assumes you have the spidev library installed. If it's not installed, you can get it from the Raspberry Pi OS repositories using the following command:

```sh
