This code uses the POSIX serial driver library for UART communication, librt for real-time GPIO access, and the standard C library for file I/O and time manipulation. It initializes the UART, sets up a thread to read and process radar data, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to gracefully shut down the program. The code also initializes an LED connected to GPIO17 and activates it for 2 seconds when a target is detected within the specified distance threshold.

code:
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
