This code initializes the I2C bus, sets up the VL53L4CX sensor, and polls its interrupt status register every 500ms. When a valid measurement is available, it logs the microsecond-precision timestamp and distance to the console. The code handles errors, skips a cycle without reporting an error if the interrupt status bit is not set after the poll, and prints an error to stderr for transient I2C communication failures while aborting cleanly for initialization failures. The program also installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that clean up the I2C handle and exit with return 0.

