This code initializes the fan GPIO, opens the I2C bus, and sets up a circular buffer for storing readings. It reads the temperature every 2 seconds, controls the fan based on the temperature, and prints the timestamped reading to stdout. The program also handles errors, retries failed I2C transactions, and degrades gracefully when the sensor is absent. It also handles SIGINT by turning the fan off, closing the I2C handle, and invoking the library's call() function before exiting.

To compile the code, you can use:

```sh
gcc -o si7021_temp_fan_monitor si7021_temp_fan_monitor.c -lgpiod -lrt
```

Don't forget to install the required libraries:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev librt-dev
```

