This code initializes the I2C bus, reads temperature data from the TMP117 sensor, stores it in a circular buffer, and logs the buffer to a file on program termination. It also handles graceful shutdown on SIGINT or SIGTERM signals. Make sure to install libgpiod and pigpio libraries before compiling the code.

To compile the code, use:

```sh
gcc -o temp_sensor temp_sensor.c -lgpiod -lrt
```

Then run the compiled binary:

```sh
./temp_sensor
```

