This code initializes the I2C bus, sets up a GPIO line for resetting the TMP117 sensor, and reads temperature data from the sensor once per second. It logs the temperature data to a file named `temperature_log.txt` in the specified format. The program handles errors related to I2C communication, sensor absence, and bus errors, and it attempts to re-initialize the I2C handle up to three consecutive times on failure before exiting. The program also processes negative temperature values and closes the I2C handle and terminates the driver cleanly on receipt of SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

