This code reads the temperature from an LM75B sensor connected to the I2C bus, stores the last 60 samples in a circular buffer, computes the running average, and drives a cooling fan connected to GPIO18 (BCM) with hysteresis so that the fan is turned on when the average exceeds 28.0 °C and turned off when it falls below 26.0 °C. The program handles errors and retries on the next cycle without crashing. It also handles SIGINT or SIGTERM by stopping the fan, closing the I2C handle, and terminating the driver library cleanly.

