This code initializes the I2C bus, opens the GPIO line, opens the log file, and enters an infinite loop that triggers a measurement when the GPIO line rises, reads the data, validates the CRC, and logs the data to a CSV file. It also handles errors and exits gracefully on SIGINT.

Please ensure to adjust the sensor's I2C address, GPIO line name, and other constants according to your specific hardware setup. Also, don't forget to install libgpiod and pigpio libraries on your Raspberry Pi before compiling the code.

To compile the code, use:

```sh
gcc -o hvac_monitor hvac_monitor.c -lgpiod -lpthread
```

Then run the compiled binary with:

```sh
