This program initializes the GPIO lines, sets up the callback for the sensors, and continuously monitors the sensors every 100ms. If either sensor reads HIGH continuously for more than 2 seconds, it activates the alarm. When both sensors return to LOW, it deactivates the alarm. The program logs ISO-8601 timestamps for tilt-start, threshold-exceeded, and tilt-end events to the `bridge_integrity.log` file.

The program also handles errors during driver library initialization, log file opening, and API call return values. It implements clean shutdown handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM that deactivates the alarm, closes the log file, calls the library's API cleanup, and guarantees the alarm is off on all exit paths.

