This code initializes the GPIO line for the WS2812B LED strip, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and enters an infinite loop that reads the ambient light, computes the brightness, and drives the LED strip. If the I2C communication with the VEML7700 sensor fails, it retries up to three times with a 100ms delay between attempts. If all retries fail, it logs an error and continues. The code also releases the GPIO line, closes the I2C file descriptor, and turns off the LED strip before exiting when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

