This code initializes the GPIO lines for the flame sensor, buzzer, and LED. It performs a startup self-test by blinking the LED and reading the flame sensor five times. If all five reads indicate a flame, it signals an error and exits with code 1. After the self-test, it enters a main loop that polls the flame sensor every 50ms. When a LOW is observed, the buzzer and LED are turned on continuously until a subsequent read returns HIGH, at which point they are turned off. The program logs events with timestamps.

The code also includes a log function that runs in a separate thread and logs events to the console. On normal termination or receipt of SIGINT, the GPIO lines are cleaned up.

