This code initializes the GPIO pins for I2C communication using libgpiod, opens the I2C device, checks the sensor identity, initializes the device, opens the log file, installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and continuously polls the accelerometer at roughly 100 Hz. When a tilt exceeding 45 degrees is detected, it appends a line to the fall_log.txt file containing a timestamp and the three raw values. The program handles errors and releases resources on all exit paths.

