This code initializes the GPIO pins, sets up the PWM for the buzzer, and creates an ISR to play the melody. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to perform a clean shutdown. The button debouncing is handled by the libgpiod library.

Make sure to compile the code with the following command:

```sh
gcc -o doorbell doorbell.c -lrt -lpthread -lgpiod -lrt -lpthread -lwiringPiDev
```

Please note that the wiringPiDev library is not actually used in this code, but it is required for the linker to find the spidev library. You can remove it if you don't have wiringPi installed.

Also, the melody is a simple one, and you can replace it with your desired melody. The melody is represented as an array of durations in milliseconds.

