This program reads edge events from an SW-420 vibration sensor module connected to GPIO17 (physical pin 11) on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It maintains a sliding window of the last five events and prints an "EARTHQUAKE ALERT" message if there are three or more HIGH events. The program also logs every edge event to a file named `vibration_events.log`.

The program handles errors gracefully, installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler, and releases the GPIO line and closes the log file on exit.

