This code reads the X, Y, and Z angular rates from an MPU-9250 gyroscope over SPI and logs them to a CSV file named `gyro_log.txt`. The SPI bus to use is `/dev/spidev0.0` configured at 1 MHz, mode 0, 8 bits per word, MSB first, with manual chip select on CE0 implemented via libgpiod on `/dev/gpiochip0` line offset 8 (GPIO8, BCM), asserting the chip-select line low during each transfer and de-asserting it high otherwise. The program performs a read every 10 ms and retrying up to three times on any SPI communication error. It writes each record as an ISO 8601 timestamp with nanosecond resolution followed by the three rate values in CSV format (timestamp,x_rate,y_rate,z_rate). The program handles persistent SPI failures by logging an error to stderr and continuing, handles file write errors gracefully, and performs proper error checking on all system and library calls. It runs indefinitely until interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM, at which point it cleans up the SPI device, GPIO line, and closes the log file.

