This program will run indefinitely, monitoring the light sensor and controlling the LED strip based on the lux value. It logs each sensor reading and relay state change to the specified log file. The program safely releases all resources on exit, including graceful shutdown when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

I'll provide a simple example using the `libgpiod` library. This code assumes you have libgpiod installed on your Raspberry Pi. If not, you can install it using the following command:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev
```

