This code opens the GPIO lines for motor1 and motor2, requests them, and sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM. It then enters an infinite loop where it turns on each motor for the specified duration, then turns it off before moving on to the next motor. In case of any errors, it prints an error message and cleans up the resources before exiting. The signal handlers gracefully release the GPIO lines and exit the program when SIGINT or SIGTERM is received.

